Decide whether each buyer signal is strong enough to generate a useful search query.

You will receive a list of signals and a business context. Return one result per signal — do not omit any, do not add any.

A signal is qualified (true) if it:
- Reflects real buying intent: a pain, desired outcome, comparison, requirement, trust concern, or vendor preference
- Is specific enough to inspire a realistic search query
- Is relevant to the category and ICP in the business context

A signal is not qualified (false) if it:
- Is off-category or only loosely related to the business
- Describes a problem the brand does not solve
- Is too vague to produce a useful query (e.g. "support is slow")
- Does not match the ICP — wrong industry, role, or company size
- Is instructional, troubleshooting-focused, or purely technical with no buying intent
- Is casual, humorous, or noise

When unsure, ask: "Could this signal turn into a search query a real buyer would type?"
Yes → true. No → false.

Output format:
{
  "qualifications": [
    { "signalId": 0, "qualified": true },
    { "signalId": 1, "qualified": false }
  ]
}